The IITs are quietly sitting on some of the most underused real estate in the country that can be made into a RAM mandir.

A quick look at the holy land, aka campuses:

@IITKgp: 2,100 acres. Four times the size of Monaco.
@IITKanpur: 1,055 acres.
@IITGuwahati: 700 acres on the banks of the Brahmaputra.
@iitmadras: 620 acres, most of it protected forest with actual deer.
@iitbombay: 550 acres, wedged between two lakes, in Powai’s priciest land.
@iitdelhi: 325 acres. Three times the size of Vatican City.
@IITBHU_Varanasi: 1,300-acre campus in literally the holy city. You do not even need the metaphor here.

Now here's my modest proposal. Carve out just 5% of each campus that's unused. We have all seen the deserted, dead parts of our huge IIT campus that no one steps foot on.

Hand it to NVIDIA, Google, or Microsoft to build a data center. Take rent, take a cut of the compute, take a few thousand free GPU hours for research while you are at it.

What happens next?
→ IITs stop begging for grants.
→ Student fees drop.
→ R&D budgets triple and infrastructure overhauls.
→ Professors skip the political circus and get more time for research.
→ The mess food finally becomes edible.

We build a temple that's climate-controlled, fiercely guarded, worshipped by trillion-dollar companies, and it runs entirely on RAM. Pilgrims (venture capitalists) travel great distances to kneel before it. 

Nvidia is the high priest. Give it an offer, and it will gladly & loudly say: Jai Shree RAM

